  "contextText": "Sasha wants to walk us through changes in the Lambda engineering org.",
  "hasTranscript": true,
  "speakers": [
    {
      "id": "m09-spk-a",
      "label": "A",
      "displayName": "Alma Mockwell"
    },
    {
      "id": "m09-spk-b",
      "label": "B",
      "displayName": "Sasha Example"
    },
    {
      "id": "m09-spk-c",
      "label": "C",
      "displayName": "Tobín Dummyson"
    },
    {
      "id": "m09-spk-d",
      "label": "D",
      "displayName": "Otis Dummyson"
    }
  ],
  "segments": [
    {
      "id": "m09-s001",
      "speakerId": "m09-spk-a",
      "startMs": 0,
      "endMs": 7060,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Thanks for setting this up, Sasha. You said there were some org changes we should know about."
    },
    {
      "id": "m09-s002",
      "speakerId": "m09-spk-b",
      "startMs": 7310,
      "endMs": 15130,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Yes, a few. First, I want to introduce Otis Dummyson. Otis joined us in February as Head of Platform."
    },
    {
      "id": "m09-s003",
      "speakerId": "m09-spk-d",
      "startMs": 15380,
      "endMs": 20540,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Hi everyone. I've been reading the pilot updates, nice work so far."
    },
    {
      "id": "m09-s004",
      "speakerId": "m09-spk-b",
      "startMs": 20790,
      "endMs": 25950,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Second, some good news. Tobín was promoted to Staff Engineer this month."
    },
    {
      "id": "m09-s005",
      "speakerId": "m09-spk-a",
      "startMs": 26200,
      "endMs": 28320,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Congratulations, Tobín, well deserved."
    },
    {
      "id": "m09-s006",
      "speakerId": "m09-spk-c",
      "startMs": 28570,
      "endMs": 35250,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Thank you. Not much changes day to day, but I'll have more say in the architecture."
    },
    {
      "id": "m09-s007",
      "speakerId": "m09-spk-b",
      "startMs": 35500,
      "endMs": 42560,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Third, and this affects you more directly: Lorne Testcase is moving to lead our robotics research group."
    },
    {
      "id": "m09-s008",
      "speakerId": "m09-spk-a",
      "startMs": 42810,
      "endMs": 46070,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "So who does Tobín report to now?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m09-s009",
      "speakerId": "m09-spk-b",
      "startMs": 46320,
      "endMs": 53000,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Tobín reported to Lorne until the end of March. From April he reports to Otis instead."
    },
    {
      "id": "m09-s010",
      "speakerId": "m09-spk-d",
      "startMs": 53250,
      "endMs": 61450,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "And the pilot's platform work moves under my team at the same time, so I'm your escalation point from April."
    },
    {
      "id": "m09-s011",
      "speakerId": "m09-spk-a",
      "startMs": 61700,
      "endMs": 67620,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "That's helpful to know. Do we need to change anything in how we work?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m09-s012",
      "speakerId": "m09-spk-d",
      "startMs": 67870,
      "endMs": 75310,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "One thing. I'd like a joint on-call rotation between Larkspur and my team once the pilot goes live."
    },
    {
      "id": "m09-s013",
      "speakerId": "m09-spk-a",
      "startMs": 75560,
      "endMs": 78440,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Makes sense. Who sets that up?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m09-s014",
      "speakerId": "m09-spk-d",
      "startMs": 78690,
      "endMs": 83850,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I'll set up the joint on-call rotation with Larkspur by April 1."
    },
    {
      "id": "m09-s015",
      "speakerId": "m09-spk-b",
      "startMs": 84100,
      "endMs": 89640,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Until then, whoever's on call on the platform team can handle anything urgent."
    },
    {
      "id": "m09-s016",
      "speakerId": "m09-spk-a",
      "startMs": 89890,
      "endMs": 94290,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Good. Otis, how do you like to work with vendors?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m09-s017",
      "speakerId": "m09-spk-d",
      "startMs": 94540,
      "endMs": 102360,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Honestly, I prefer a written proposal a day before any meeting. I'd rather read than be walked through slides."
    },
    {
      "id": "m09-s018",
      "speakerId": "m09-spk-a",
      "startMs": 102610,
      "endMs": 104730,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Easy. We'll send pre-reads."
    },
    {
      "id": "m09-s019",
      "speakerId": "m09-spk-c",
      "startMs": 104980,
      "endMs": 111660,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Lorne will still be around, by the way. The research group is on the same floor."
    },
    {
      "id": "m09-s020",
      "speakerId": "m09-spk-b",
      "startMs": 111910,
      "endMs": 117830,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Right, and she'll want to hear how the pilot goes. It started under her."
    },
    {
      "id": "m09-s021",
      "speakerId": "m09-spk-a",
      "startMs": 118080,
      "endMs": 122100,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I'll make sure she gets the Friday updates too."
    },
    {
      "id": "m09-s022",
      "speakerId": "m09-spk-b",
      "startMs": 122350,
      "endMs": 129030,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Good. So to confirm: Otis is your escalation point from April, and Tobín stays technical lead."
    },
    {
      "id": "m09-s023",
      "speakerId": "m09-spk-c",
      "startMs": 129280,
      "endMs": 132540,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Yes, nothing changes on the technical side."
    },
    {
      "id": "m09-s024",
      "speakerId": "m09-spk-a",
      "startMs": 132790,
      "endMs": 135670,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Thanks Sasha, that's a clear picture."
    }
  ],
  "note": {
    "version": 1,
    "body": "# Lambda platform org update\n\n**Date:** March 5\n**Attendees:** Alma Mockwell (Larkspur Labs), Sasha Example (Org Lambda Robotics), Tobín Dummyson (Org Lambda Robotics), Otis Dummyson (Org Lambda Robotics)\n\n## Summary\n\nSasha Example walked us through three changes in the Org Lambda Robotics engineering organisation and what they mean for the pick-path pilot.\n\n## Changes\n\n1. **Otis Dummyson** joined Lambda in February as **Head of Platform**.\n2. **Tobín Dummyson** was promoted to **Staff Engineer** this month. Day-to-day work is unchanged, but he will have more say in architecture.\n3. **Lorne Testcase** is moving to lead the robotics research group. Tobín reported to Lorne until the end of March; from April he reports to Otis.\n\n## Decisions\n\n- The pilot's platform work moves under Otis's team from April. Otis becomes Larkspur's escalation point; Tobín stays technical lead.\n\n## Action items\n\n- **Otis Dummyson** — set up a joint on-call rotation between Larkspur and the platform team by April 1.\n- **Alma Mockwell** — add Lorne Testcase to the Friday update distribution; send Otis written pre-reads before meetings.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Until the rotation exists, whoever's on call on the platform team handles anything urgent.\n- Otis prefers a written proposal a day before any meeting rather than being walked through slides.\n- Lorne's research group is on the same floor, and she will want to hear how the pilot goes since it started under her.\n"
  },
